  "specReview": [
    "Migration003 rebuilds approvals with identical columns, default, primary key and two FK constraints, removing only UNIQUE(target_kind,target_id,target_hash,decision). INSERT SELECT copies every approval row.",
    "Generic records, historical natural keys, record_refs and takes are not updated or deleted. Approval references in take/record_refs point to generic records rather than the rebuilt approvals table.",
    "Future appendApproval uses r.id for natural_key, preserving existing getApproval replay port and identity constraints while enabling distinct approve/reject/approve command IDs for the same target/hash.",
    "Migration registry adds exact version3/name. SupportedStorageSchemaVersion adds literal3 and keeps future4 rejected; financial records and project-read versions unchanged."
  ],
  "codeQualityAndMaterialRisk": [
    "Rebuild executes inside the existing immediate migration transaction with foreign keys enabled and schema_migrations recorded atomically; startup rollback/error handling remains unchanged.",
    "New real-v2 fixture observes migration and reopen, historical approval/take rows and refs, historical natural key retention, three ascending decision times, command-ID natural keys, integrity_check and foreign_key_check.",
    "Existing migration/concurrent-startup tests only update expected schema3 and future4 history; no skips, deleted assertions, relaxed bounds or startup algorithm change.",
    "No blocking material risk identified in the five-file owned storage slice. Existing2000ms lock timing test once failed at2001ms and subsequently passed; its threshold and algorithm were not changed by this candidate."
  ],
